136
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:04,880
If I go back home, who knows what they'll do to me!

137
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:09,060
Then again, am I really capable of living out here on my own?

138
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:15,500
Well, it's one of you pretty young things from the Whiteleaf family!

139
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:18,880
You all alone out here?

140
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:22,420
We're just a trio of starving bandits!

141
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,420
Can you spare something to help us?

142
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:30,680
I'm sorry, I don't have any money, so I'm afraid there isn't anything I can do for you!

143
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:32,940
Well, your family has plenty!

144
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,040
Maybe we can just take you!

145
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:36,760
I'm helpless!

146
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,320
Come on, let's grab her!

147
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:38,820
Oh, no!

148
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,180
Nice lady!

149
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:47,440
Are you hurt?

150
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,120
I'm fine!

151
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:50,540
Thank you so much!

152
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:51,720
Don't get the wrong idea!

153
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:55,720
The only reason I bothered to save you was because Marie wanted me to!

154
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:57,540
Isn't she sweet?

155
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:58,380
Good girl!

156
00:07:58,820 --> 00:08:00,440
You really are an angel!

157
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,320
You know that Marie?

158
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,640
My precious, adorable little angel!

159
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,420
Thank you for helping her, big brother!

160
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,600
Of course!

161
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:09,140
Anything for you, Marie!

162
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:11,860
I didn't know siblings could be that close!

163
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:13,700
That's nice!

164
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,580
I wish I had...

165
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:16,020
Hey!

166
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,700
What are you doing out here alone?

167
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:21,300
Well, the truth is...

168
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,340
You should probably go back home now.

169
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,260
You ran away?

170
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:31,420
If you did it because of something stupid, you might as well turn around.

171
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:37,940
Trust me, you'll never survive in this rotten excuse for a world if you don't have the resolve to fight tooth and nail for the life you want.

172
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:43,580
